  "graph": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "1",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "Study: a clip launcher and looper (clip slots, scenes, quantized launch, a loop pedal), built from today's nodes.\n\nThree tracks with two clip slots each. A slot's button arms it; at the next bar a Clock samples the armed state and the slot's Clip starts or stops, so launches land on the bar. Launching one slot disarms the other on its track, a Stop button clears a track, and a scene button launches a whole row. The Looper records the input between two bar lines into a buffer that a Sampler loops. In a render the demo arms scene 1 at the start and scene 2 at bar 5. The Session panel is the grid.\n\nWhat a launcher has that this can't: slots that show playing, armed, and stopped states; a grid with rows and columns; follow actions; overdubbing; recording a loop whose length sets the tempo. Read docs/GAPS.md."
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            0.0,
            -680.0
          ],
          "size": [
            760.0,
            270.0
          ]
        }
      },
